course: dictionary
lesson: 13876
title: Word study: killjoy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A killjoy is a person who spoils other people's fun. Context helps you spot it. «Don't be such a killjoy, it's only a game!» The speaker is cross because someone has stopped the game, so a killjoy is someone who stops people enjoying themselves.
explain: Look at the word parts: kill and joy. Joy means happiness, so a killjoy takes away the happiness. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «Don't be such a spoiler of fun, it's only a game!» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Be careful: a killjoy is not always wrong. «Tom wanted to ride his bike on the icy road. "Don't be a killjoy," he moaned. His sister was only keeping him safe.» Here the word is used unfairly, because she was being sensible. Context tells you how the speaker feels.
fact: A killjoy is a person who spoils other people's fun.
fact: Killjoy is an informal word, so you would use it in chatting with friends, not in a formal essay.
fact: Killjoy is a noun. The plural is killjoys.
fact: «Killjoy» is often said about someone who is grumpy or too strict.
fact: Sometimes a killjoy is just being sensible, such as stopping a dangerous game.
exercise: «Don't be such a killjoy, it's only a game!» What is a killjoy? | A person who wins every game | A person who makes the best cakes | A person who loves games very much | *A person who spoils other people's fun
exercise: Mia's dad turned off the music and said, «Time for bed.» Mia cried, «Dad, you're such a killjoy!» Why does Mia say this? | Because he sang the song loudly | Because he gave her a present | *Because he stopped the fun | Because he cooked her dinner
exercise: Which word means about the same as killjoy? | helper | hero | winner | *spoilsport
test: Tom's sister said, «Don't ride on the ice,» and Tom called her a killjoy. Why might she be right? | *Because the ice could be dangerous | Because Tom was winning the race | Because it was summer and very hot | Because she wanted to ride the bike too
test: What is the plural of killjoy? | killjoy's | killjoies | killjoyes | *killjoys
exam: Which sentence uses killjoy correctly? | Killjoy means a very tall tree in the park. | *«Don't be such a killjoy, Ruby, the party is only just starting!» | The killjoy baked a big chocolate cake for the party. | The killjoy is a small brown bird that sings at night.
